    <bpmn:process id="W_W622" name="W622. Mock Product Recall Exercise &amp; Recall Readiness Testing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual calendar; semi-annual for high-risk product categories
Frequency: Annual company-wide; semi-annual for paint, chemicals, electrical items
Volume: 1 company-wide mock exercise/year; 2 category-specific exercises/year
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, VP Supply Chain, LP Manager, VP Store Operations, Communications Manager, Quality Assurance Specialist, affected Category Manager
Source: workflow W622 — Mock Product Recall Exercise &amp; Recall Readiness Testing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W622_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W622_Lane1" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W622_Lane2" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W622_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W622_Lane4" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W622_Lane5" name="Communications Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W622_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W622_Start7" name="Annual calendar; semi-annual for high-risk product categories">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W622_Task8" name="VP Merchandising selects mock recall scenario: (a) product category (paint…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Merchandising selects mock recall scenario: (a) product category (paint, electrical, lumber treatment, appliance), (b) recall reason (safety defect, regulatory non-compliance, contamination), (c) scope (nationwide or regional), (d) exercise timeline (target: 48-hour completion)
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W622_Task9" name="VP Supply Chain identifies affected SKU(s) and traces forward in ERP: (a) total…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Supply Chain identifies affected SKU(s) and traces forward in ERP: (a) total quantity manufactured/procured, (b) all locations holding stock (DCs, stores, in-transit, ecommerce inventory), (c) all customer transactions (POS sales, ecommerce orders, wholesale) with customer contact details for notification
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W622_Task10" name="System executes simulated recall actions: (a) block affected SKU at all POS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System executes simulated recall actions: (a) block affected SKU at all POS terminals (200 stores), (b) remove from ecommerce and marketplace listings, (c) quarantine in-transit shipments, (d) flag DC stock for hold; all actions timestamped for speed measurement
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min (simulated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W622_Task11" name="VP Store Operations coordinates simulated store-level actions: (a) Stock…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: VP Store Operations coordinates simulated store-level actions: (a) Stock Associates locate and quarantine affected product on shelves, (b) customer-facing signage posted, (c) Store Manager confirms quarantine completion via mobile app; time-to-completion measured per store
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 4 hours (simulated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W622_Task12" name="Communications Manager drafts simulated customer notification: (a) press…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Communications Manager drafts simulated customer notification: (a) press release, (b) social media announcement, (c) customer email/SMS to affected transaction customers, (d) DTI/FDA notification (simulated); reviews with Legal Counsel for accuracy and liability considerations
Responsible (R): Communications Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W622_Task13" name="VP Merchandising compiles mock recall performance metrics: (a) time from…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: VP Merchandising compiles mock recall performance metrics: (a) time from decision to POS block, (b) time from decision to ecommerce removal, (c) store quarantine completion rate at 4/12/24/48 hours, (d) customer notification completion rate, (e) percentage of affected stock accounted for (target: 100% within 48 hours)
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W622_Task14" name="Post-exercise debrief (within 1 week): all participants review performance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-exercise debrief (within 1 week): all participants review performance metrics, identify gaps in process or system, document lessons learned, and create improvement action items with owners and deadlines
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W622_Task15" name="Improvement actions tracked in project management system (per W128); system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Improvement actions tracked in project management system (per W128); system updates made to recall workflow (W29) based on findings; next exercise scenario designed to test improved areas
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W622_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W622_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W622_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W622_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-243 (ensure controlled execution — Demand Forecasting &amp; S&amp;OP (PA-02.1).) | - operational: recall-exercise control — exercise scheduled in low-traffic windows, test-store scope approved by VP Merchandising, traceability gaps logged to CAPA before live-recall readiness sign-off, scenario variance documented per exercise
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W622_Assoc18" sourceRef="W622_Annotation17" targetRef="W622_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow19" sourceRef="W622_Start7" targetRef="W622_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow20" sourceRef="W622_Task8" targetRef="W622_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow21" sourceRef="W622_Task9" targetRef="W622_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow22" sourceRef="W622_Task10" targetRef="W622_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow23" sourceRef="W622_Task11" targetRef="W622_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow24" sourceRef="W622_Task12" targetRef="W622_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow25" sourceRef="W622_Task13" targetRef="W622_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow26" sourceRef="W622_Task14" targetRef="W622_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W622_Flow27" sourceRef="W622_Task15" targetRef="W622_End16" />
    </bpmn:process>
