    <bpmn:process id="W_W1356" name="W1356. Store-Level Demand Sensing &amp; Local Event-Driven Forecast Adjustment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Identification of a local event (festival, LGU infrastructure project, school construction, competitor store closure) that will impact demand at specific stores
Frequency: Ad-hoc; ~10–20 local events/month across 200 stores that warrant forecast adjustment
Volume: Each event affects 1–5 stores; adjustment covers 50–500 SKUs per event
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Store Manager (intelligence source), Regional Manager, Supply Planning Manager
Source: workflow W1356 — Store-Level Demand Sensing &amp; Local Event-Driven Forecast Adjustment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1356_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1356_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1356_Lane2" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1356_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1356_Lane4" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1356_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1356_Start6" name="Identification of a local event (festival, LGU infrastructure project, school…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1356_Task7" name="Store Manager or Regional Manager identifies local event that will impact…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Store Manager or Regional Manager identifies local event that will impact demand; submits event notification via Store Manager mobile app with: event type, expected impact (high/medium/low), affected categories, estimated duration
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1356_Task8" name="Merchandise Planner receives event notification; assesses credibility and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Merchandise Planner receives event notification; assesses credibility and magnitude by cross-referencing with regional sales trends and publicly available information (LGU announcements, local news)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1356_Task9" name="Planner models demand impact: applies uplift percentage to affected SKU…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Planner models demand impact: applies uplift percentage to affected SKU categories for the specific stores during the event window; uses historical analogs from similar past events (e.g., previous subdivision launches)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30–60 min/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1356_Task10" name="System generates adjusted replenishment parameters for affected stores…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System generates adjusted replenishment parameters for affected stores: increases ROP and safety stock for high-impact SKUs; suppresses auto-replenishment for categories expected to decline (e.g., garden products during a construction event)
Responsible (R): System / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1356_Task11" name="Supply Planning Manager reviews significant adjustments (&gt; 30% uplift or &gt; PHP…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Supply Planning Manager reviews significant adjustments (&gt; 30% uplift or &gt; PHP 200K incremental inventory); approves or modifies
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1356_Task12" name="Adjusted replenishment parameters flow into auto-replenishment cycle (W2A)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Adjusted replenishment parameters flow into auto-replenishment cycle (W2A); system generates larger or earlier POs/transfer orders for affected stores
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1356_Task13" name="Post-event: Planner compares adjusted forecast vs. actual sales; records…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-event: Planner compares adjusted forecast vs. actual sales; records accuracy outcome in event library for future reference
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1356_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1356_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1356_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
