    <bpmn:process id="W_W1533" name="W1533. S&amp;OP Monthly Consensus Demand Review, Cross-Functional Alignment &amp; Supply Plan Ratification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly S&amp;OP calendar (typically 2nd week of month for M+1 planning)
Frequency: Monthly (12 cycles/year)
Volume: 1 consensus meeting per month covering all 35,000 active SKUs across the 13 departments/~40 categories (profile §6.2)
Owner: VP Supply Chain
Participants: VP Supply Chain, VP Merchandising, Category Managers, Demand Planner, Supply Planner, Finance Controller, DC Operations Manager
Source: workflow W1533 — S&amp;OP Monthly Consensus Demand Review, Cross-Functional Alignment &amp; Supply Plan Ratification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1533_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1533_Lane1" name="Demand Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1533_Lane2" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1533_Lane3" name="Supply Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1533_Lane4" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1533_Lane5" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1533_Lane6" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1533_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1533_Start8" name="Monthly S&amp;OP calendar (typically 2nd week of month for M+1 planning)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1533_Task9" name="Demand review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Demand review: Demand Planner presents statistical forecast by category with accuracy metrics (MAPE, bias); highlights significant changes from prior month (new product launches, seasonal shifts, promotional impacts)
Responsible (R): Demand Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1533_Task10" name="Merchandising input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Merchandising input: Category Managers provide qualitative demand adjustments — upcoming promotions (W13), new store openings (W16), product discontinuations (W68), vendor supply risk, competitor activity; system applies overrides to statistical forecast
Responsible (R): Category Managers
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1533_Task11" name="Supply constraint review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Supply constraint review: Supply Planner presents current supply position — open PO status, import container pipeline, vendor capacity constraints, DC throughput capacity; identifies constrained categories requiring allocation (W105)
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1533_Task12" name="Financial reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Financial reconciliation: Finance Controller compares consensus demand plan against annual budget and working capital targets; flags categories where planned inventory exceeds approved OTB (Open-to-Buy); provides margin impact assessment of demand changes
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1533_Task13" name="Consensus decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consensus decision: VP Supply Chain facilitates resolution of demand-supply imbalances; approves final demand numbers by category; authorizes exception procurement (import expediting, emergency POs); defers unresolved items to executive review
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1533_Task14" name="Supply plan ratification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Supply plan ratification: System generates ratified supply plan — PO release schedule, transfer order plan, allocation rules — distributed to procurement (W2), DC operations (W584), and logistics (W196) for execution
Responsible (R): System / Supply Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1533_Task15" name="KPI review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: KPI review: Review prior month S&amp;OP performance — forecast accuracy by category, service level achievement, inventory days of supply, fill rate, promotional stock availability
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1533_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1533_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1533_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1533_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-172 (ensure demand-plan integrity &amp; replenishment authorization.) | - operational: VP Supply Chain review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: VP Supply Chain</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1533_Assoc18" sourceRef="W1533_Annotation17" targetRef="W1533_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
