    <bpmn:process id="W_W5509" name="W5509. Unfulfilled-Demand &amp; Lost-Sales Capture, Substitution Analytics &amp; Replenishment Feedback" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous event capture (every POS no-sale reason code, floor inquiry log, declined quotation, OOS page view); weekly analytics cycle; monthly feedback cycle
Frequency: Continuous capture; weekly review; monthly S&amp;OP feedback
Volume: ~15,000–35,000 unfulfilled-demand events captured/month chain-wide (~2–6 per store per day) across POS reason codes, floor inquiry logs, quote declines (W542), rain checks (W772), backorders (W56) and special orders (W38); estimated gross lost-sales value PHP 20–50M/month (0.4–1% of the ~PHP 5.19B monthly revenue), of which substitution and order-based recovery nets ~30–50%
Owner: Demand Planner
Participants: Demand Planner, Supply Planner, Category Manager, Merchandising Analyst, Store Manager and department staff (capture), BI Analyst, VP Supply Chain
Source: workflow W5509 — Unfulfilled-Demand &amp; Lost-Sales Capture, Substitution Analytics &amp; Replenishment Feedback</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5509_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5509_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5509_Lane2" name="Demand Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5509_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5509_Start4" name="Continuous event capture (every POS no-sale reason code, floor inquiry log, declined…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5509_Task5" name="Capture instrumentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Capture instrumentation: POS no-sale/zero-scan reason-code protocol (single-tap SKU scan-or-search when a customer asks for an item the terminal or associate cannot fulfill); sales-floor inquiry quick-log in the store mobile app by department; quotation-decline reason tagging (W542); automatic tagging of rain-check issuance (W772), backorder intake (W56) and special-order intake (W38) as unfulfilled-at-first-touch; ecommerce OOS product-page events; endless-aisle saves via vendor-direct delivery (W273) tagged as *recovered* demand
Responsible (R): System / Store Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: ~10–20 sec per captured event (absorbed at point of service)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5509_Task6" name="Daily event pipeline and classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily event pipeline and classification: events land in the demand-event fact table; deduplication (customer × SKU × store × day) prevents double-counting across channels; each event classified: (a) stocked-out — on-hand zero but active in assortment; (b) not-stocked — assortment gap at that store; (c) quantity-insufficient — partial fulfillment; (d) price-driven walk-away (distinct trigger, routes to W61/W542 analytics instead); (e) specification mismatch (routes to product feedback)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Demand Planner
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5509_Task7" name="Quantification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quantification: true lost sales = stockout duration × baseline sales velocity (W31 forecast baseline for the SKU-store) × average margin, netted for recovery (substitute SKU sold in the same basket, rain check redeemed, backorder/special order converted, vendor-direct save per W273); gross vs net split reported so recovery programs get credit
Responsible (R): System / Demand Planner
Accountable (A): Demand Planner
Duration: Automated + 1 hour/week review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5509_Task8" name="Weekly lost-sales and substitution analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Weekly lost-sales and substitution analytics: top-20 lost-sales SKU list by value with named owner and action; substitution matrix (which alternate SKUs capture which unfulfilled demand — feeding cross-sell analytics W1215 and planogram adjacency in VS-55); store/region heat maps; capture-compliance scorecard per store (captured events ÷ sampled OOS inquiries)
Responsible (R): Demand Planner / BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5509_Task9" name="Forecast feedback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Forecast feedback: unfulfilled-demand overlay into W31 manual forecast overrides (OOS periods systematically under-represent demand in pure sales history — the classic under-forecast bias) and W2A safety-stock/service-level tuning for repeat-offender SKU-locations; distinct from W1252/W1356 demand sensing (leading indicators) — this feed is *realized* unfulfilled demand
Responsible (R): Demand Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5509_Task10" name="Assortment and vendor attribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Assortment and vendor attribution: not-stocked events feed assortment review and new-item proposals (W1451 category analytics; item-master additions per W252); stocked-out events attribute root cause — vendor lead-time failures to the VS-03.3 RCA and W44 scorecard, allocation/DC issues to W1535 rebalancing triggers
Responsible (R): Demand Planner / Merchandising Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5509_Task11" name="Monthly S&amp;OP input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly S&amp;OP input: lost-sales trend, recovery rate and capture-compliance reported in the W1533 consensus review; typhoon-season and ber-month pre-positioning (W1355) uses historical surge lost-sales by region to size buffer buys
Responsible (R): Demand Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Part of monthly S&amp;OP pack</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5509_Task12" name="Quarterly instrumentation audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly instrumentation audit: capture-completeness sampling correlated with mystery-shopping observations (VS-146) and W884 data-quality monitoring; target-setting (reduce net captured lost sales 10–15% YoY); protocol updates where classification drift is found
Responsible (R): Demand Planner / BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5509_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5509_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5509_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5509_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-243 (ensure controlled execution — Demand Forecasting &amp; S&amp;OP (PA-02.1).) | - operational: dedupe key enforced at ingest; gross-vs-net recovery split reported; capture-compliance scorecard with Store Manager review; no-PII design reviewed annually with the VS-91 program
Owner: Demand Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5509_Assoc15" sourceRef="W5509_Annotation14" targetRef="W5509_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow16" sourceRef="W5509_Start4" targetRef="W5509_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow17" sourceRef="W5509_Task5" targetRef="W5509_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow18" sourceRef="W5509_Task6" targetRef="W5509_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow19" sourceRef="W5509_Task7" targetRef="W5509_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow20" sourceRef="W5509_Task8" targetRef="W5509_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow21" sourceRef="W5509_Task9" targetRef="W5509_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow22" sourceRef="W5509_Task10" targetRef="W5509_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow23" sourceRef="W5509_Task11" targetRef="W5509_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5509_Flow24" sourceRef="W5509_Task12" targetRef="W5509_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
